<title>FRANCE: EU approves Beghin-Say's Actilight.</title>
<headline>EU approves Beghin-Say's Actilight.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agribusiness group Eridania Beghin-Say said on Wednesday the European Commission's scientific food committee has approved use of its Actilight product for human consumption.</p>
<p>Actilight is produced and marketed in Europe by Beghin Meiji Industries, part of the Beghin-Say group. The product is based on beet sugar and has properties to stimulate and balance intestinal flora, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Beghin-Say has built a production unit for Actilight in the Paris region, capable of producing several thousand tonnes a year.</p>
</text>
